<title>USA: Hughes sees sales doubling by 2001 - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Hughes sees sales doubling by 2001 - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new Hughes Electronics Corp should more than double in size to at least $10 billion in sales by the year 2001, Chief Executive C. Michael Armstrong said in an interview published Monday.</p>
<p>Armstrong told the Wall Street Journal that he expects sales for Hughes's space and communications business to grow at a minimum rate of 20 percent a year for the next five years.</p>
<p>He said the systems Hughes wants to build and expand are high risk and may not unfold &quot;exactly the way we plan.&quot;</p>
</text>
